<title>USA: Constellation names Baltimore Gas exec CFO.</title>
<headline>Constellation names Baltimore Gas exec CFO.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Constellation Energy Corp, the company arising from the merger of Potomac Electric Power Co and Baltimore Gas and Electric Co, said on Monday it named David Brune as senior vice president and chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Brune, employed by Baltimore Gas for 21 years, will replace Charles Shivery, who was named chief executive officer of Constellation Power Source Inc, Baltimore Gas's new power marketing subsidiary.  </p>
<p>Brune served as Baltimore Gas's general counsel since 1984, the company said.</p>
<p>In March, Baltimore Gas and Potomac Electric shareholders approved a proposed merger, but the transaction is still pending regulatory approval.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
